## Post-restart consumer recovery — 2026-11-07

T013 is complete for the current Ox-only boundary. The first current execution
exposed an unregistered project append and two obsolete native-OSV expectations.
The exact ownership successor and partial-copy consumers are repaired; native OSV
is refused without execution. Four focused cases reject unknown bytes, active
downgrades, corrupted/missing registries/reviews/preimages and symlink escapes.
The fast suite passes 112 cases (107 passed, five Docker opt-ins skipped).
Independent governance-only check-ox and SDD --require-fresh both exit 0;
maintenance reconstructs 439/439 historical inputs. No Docker/external write.

Affected ownership observations remain verbatim in historical_evidence, with
new recovery evidence and current contract bindings. AC-05/06 retain bounded
consumer acceptance; AC-01..04 remain INCONCLUSIVE and AC-07 UNVERIFIED. Prior
scanner and full executions are not approval of this changed ownership contract.
See docs/validation/scanner-toolbox-ownership/recovery/report.md and independent/.
